"DATA","ID128A","9.30","16.70","Very stiff light grey CLAY with bivalve fragmented shells. Discontinuities: 1. Abundant sub-vertical fissures, planar, smooth, incipient. 2. Sub-horizontal fissures, very closely spaced, planar undulating, smooth incipient, extremely closely spaced at 10.8 to 12.3m. Cone loss at 12.3 to 13.1m Becomes more fossiliferous after 13.1 as bivalve shells and ammonite shells, gastropods and small coral pieces become abundant. Slightly pyritised ammonite at 15.2 ammonite is 80mm","201","OC","","","","","","",""
