"DATA","ID128B","18.72","25.25","Stiff to very stiff grey CLAY. Slightly fossiliferous (broken bivalves, ammonite, gastropod shells) extremely fossiliferous at 23.2 to 23.35 (mostly pyritised ammonite). Discontinuities 1. Sub-horizontal fissure, medium spaced throughout but two closely spaced at 17.7 to 17.9, very closely spaced at 19.15 to 19.35m, five extremely closely spaced at 19.45 to 19.52m, four extremely closely spaced at 22.55 to 22.60m, planar, smooth, incipient. 2. Large subvertical fissures (potential shears) at 19.05 to 19.65m, 20.05 to 20.25m, 20.55 to 21.5m, 21.7 to 22.20m, 24.6 to 24.9m, planar, smooth polished incipient.","201","OC","","","","","","",""
