"DATA","ID202","4.20","10.80","Stiff dark grey silty CLAY with gravel sized phosphate nodules between 4.50 to 5.70m with rare belemnite and nodule local fossils and some broken bivalve shells. Becoming very stiff rock like at 6.0 to 6.3m and at 10.60m Discontinuities: 1. 0 to 80° fissures medium spaced, planar, smooth incipient. 2. Few subvertical fissure, planar smooth incipient. ","202","OC","Bedrock","","","","","",""
"DATA","ID202","10.80","19.80","Stiff to very stiff, grey silty CLAY. Fossiliferous with bivalves, brachiopods, gastropods. Intro of nodular coral fossils at 13.70 and disappearance at 15.00. Introduction of slightly pyritised ammonites at 14.30m. Large culmination of fossils at 17.40 to 17.60m solidified to a weak to medium strong rock. Discontinuities 1. Sub-horizontal fissures, medium spaced, planar, smooth, incipient 2. Few small subvertical fissures <50mm as viewed in core, planar smooth incipient. 3. Two sub-vertical fissures one at 18.50 to 18.75m  and one at 19.25 to 19.40m. Planar, smooth to polished incipient.","202","OC","Bedrock","","","","","",""
