"DATA","ID262","5.70","11.70","Very stiff grey silty CLAY with rare small bivalves (20mm-40mm), nodular coral and unidentifiable fossil fragments  Discontinuity Set 1:  sub-horizontal fissures, medium spaced, planar, smooth, incipient  Discontinuity Set 2:  sub-vertical fissures, planar, smooth, incipient","202","OC","","","","","","",""
"DATA","ID262","11.70","12.00","Firm to stiff grey slightly sandy silty CLAY.  Sand is fine to coarse","207","OC","","","","","","",""
"DATA","ID262","12.00","16.27","Very stiff grey silty CLAY with rare bivalves, nodular coral and unidentified fragmented fossil and belemnites.  Some fossils quite pyritised.  Small amount of black lignite at 14.90m  Discontinuity Set 1:  sub-horizontal fissures, medium spaced, planar, smooth, incipient  Discontinuity Set 2:  sub-vertical fissures, medium spaced, planar, smooth, incipient  Discontinuity Set 3:  potential shear surfaces.  One at 13.30m - 13.40m, sub-vertical, planar, polished, incipient.  Another at 13.70m - 13.85m, sub-vertical, planar, polished, incipient and perpendicular to each other.  Another at 15.00m - 15.10m, sub-vertical, planar, polished, incipient.  Another at 16.20m - 16.27m, sub-vertical, planar, polished, incipient","202","OC","","","","","","",""
"DATA","ID262","16.27","19.70","Very stiff, thickly laminated, dark grey silty CLAY.  Fossiliferous with numerous broken bivalve shells and gastropods and rare ammonites, some of which are slightly pyritised and nodules of coral","202","OC","","","","","","",""
