"DATA","ID307","0.70","5.60","Very stiff mottled brown grey slightly sandy slightly gravelly silty CLAY. Sand is fine to coarse. Gravel is fine to coarse of mixed lithology predominantly chalk and flint. ","211","GT-C","","","","","","",""
"DATA","ID307","5.60","15.73","Very stiff dark brownish grey slightly gravelly CLAY. Gravel is fine to coarse subrounded to rounded of mixed lithologies predominantly white chalk with flint and sandstone. Traces of shell fragments, bivalves and possible coral Discontinuity Set 1: Subvertical fissures, undulating, smooth, incipient. Discontinuity Set 2: 0 to 30 degree fissures, medium spaced, planar, rough incipient. ","204","GT-C","","","","","","",""
"DATA","ID307","15.73","25.00","Very stiff dark greenish grey and brownish grey silty CLAY with rare fossils of ammonites and shell fragments. Traces of fine gravel sized pyrite.   Discontinuity Set 1: Subhorizontal fissures, very closely becoming closely spaced below 17.0 cm undulating, smooth, incipient. Discontinuity Set 2: Subvertical fissures, planar, smooth, incipient. Discontinuity Set 3: 15.70m to 17.0m 40 to 50 degree shears closely spaced becoming medium spaced below 16.35m, planar, occasionally undulating, polished typically closed occasionally incipient.  Discontinuity Set 4: 17.0m to 23.0m subvertical shears, typically planar occasionally undulating polished, incipient.  Discontinuity Set 5: 18.50m to 21.50m  40 to 50 degrees shears, closely spaced becoming medium spaced in places, planar, polished closed.  Discontinuity Set 6: 19.65m to 19.85m one 80 degree shear, undulating rough closed.  ","202","OC","","","","","","",""
